/-!
# The canonical `ℓ`-adic cycle class system, characterized (Corollary 6.6)

This file defines the *characterized
interface* of the canonical `ℓ`-adic cycle class system of a smooth proper scheme `X` over a field
`k`, with `k̄` an algebraic closure (separable over `k`), on the carriers (Stacks Chow
groups, Stacks étale `Ext` groups with supports, the library's `ℓ`-adic cohomology
`H^{2c}(X_{k̄}, ℚ_ℓ(c))` with its `Gal(k̄/k)`-action), and proves the manuscript's own reductions
from it.

## The characterization (`CanonicalCycleSystem`)

The class of **every integral closed subscheme** `Z ⊆ X_{k̄}` of dimension `i` (codimension
`c = d - i`, every codimension) is its fundamental (Gysin) class with supports, characterized
levelwise by purity and by forgetting supports (`CanonicalCycleSystem.fundamental`):

* for every level `ℓⁿ⁺¹` there is a class with supports
  `γₙ ∈ H^{2c}_Z(X_{k̄}, ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹) = Ext^{2c}(ι_* ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹_Z, ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹_{X_{k̄}})` (`SupportExt`, the
  library's carrier of purity classes);
* **purity**: for every open `O ⊆ Z` smooth over `k̄` of dimension `i`, the restriction of `γₙ` to
  `O` (`restrictToOpen`) is a local purity class in the library's sense
  (`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.Purity.IsLocalPurityClass`; SGA 4 XVI 3.7): the
  Gysin maps `Ext^q_O(-, ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹) → Ext^{q+2c}(ι_* -, ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹)` are bijective and
  `Ext^{q}(ι_* -, ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹) = 0` for `q < 2c` — so `γₙ` is nonzero for nonempty `Z`, in **every**
  codimension;
* **forgetting supports**: `forgetSupports γₙ ∈ H^{2c}(X_{k̄}, ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹)` is the `n`-th level
  (`AbelianEtale.levelExtEquiv ∘ levelProj`) of an `ℓ`-adic class `x ∈ H^{2c}(X_{k̄}, ℤ_ℓ)`, and the
  cycle class of the Stacks Chow class `[Z] ∈ A_i(X_{k̄})` is the twisted `ℚ_ℓ`-class
  `twistMk x ∈ H^{2c}(X_{k̄}, ℚ_ℓ(c))`.

Together with `one` (the image of the identity of `ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹`), the **unit normalization**
`cl[X_{k̄}] = 1` and the **Chern normalization** (the class of `c₁(L) ∩ α`, `c₁(L) ∩ -` the Stacks
Chern cap operator, equals `cl(α) ∪ c₁(L)`, where the divisor class `c₁(L)` of an invertible
module is *defined* as the cycle class of `c₁(L) ∩ [X_{k̄}]`), this is the source's
characterization on all cycle classes. The ring structure is thus determined where it is used:
`one` is pinned by its levels, `c₁` is the cycle class of the Stacks Chern cap, and `cup` is pinned
on every pair (cycle class, divisor class) — exactly the products appearing in Zarhin's
Theorem 8.1.

The system has a global sign `ε = orientationSign : ℤˣ` relating the support-boundary and Yoneda
conventions. The manuscript's span conclusions hold for either sign.

**The Kummer orientation (`IsKummerOriented`).** A purity class is determined only up to a unit
of `ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹` per `Z`. This unit is removed by the Kummer boundary of local regular
parameters, on **charts** (`KummerChart`): a Zariski open `U ⊆ X_{k̄}` with functions
`φ₁, …, φ_c ∈ Γ(U, 𝒪_U)` such that each `i_m : W_m ⟶ U` is the *principal closed subscheme*
`V(φ_m)` (the ideal sheaf `ker i_m` **equals** the ideal sheaf generated by `φ_m`, not merely the
same zero set), the scheme-theoretic intersection `Z ∩ U` has ideal sheaf **equal** to
`(φ₁, …, φ_c)`, `X_{k̄}` is smooth of relative dimension `r + c` and `Z ∩ U` smooth of relative
dimension `r` (so the `φ_m` are transverse regular parameters), and `θ` identifies the Kummer flag
sheaf with the extension by zero of `Z ∩ U` compatibly with the units. On every chart the
restriction of `γₙ` to `Z ∩ U` is `ε^c` times the library's raw Yoneda flag
`KummerFlag.kummerFlagClass` (the
Yoneda product of the Kummer boundaries `κ(φ_m)` of the units `φ_m|_{D(φ_m)}`, `μ_{ℓⁿ⁺¹} ≅ ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹`
through the compatible root system `ζ`, which also identifies `ℚ_ℓ(c)` with `ℚ_ℓ`). The equations
`ker i_m = (φ_m)` specify the principal closed subschemes, and `Z ∩ U` is reduced since `Z` is
integral. For every integral cycle `Z`, every level and every open `O ⊆ Z` smooth of the correct
relative dimension, `CanonicalCycleSystem.charts` covers `O` by the opens of Kummer charts.
`CanonicalCycleSystemExists` includes this cover (EGA IV₄ 17.12.1–2 and SGA 4 VIII 1.1).
Since a class with supports is determined by its restriction to a dense open of `Z` (standard
excision plus the vanishing below degree `2c`), this pins `γₙ` and hence
`clBar` — in particular `c₁(L)` — **with no scalar or unit choice left**, for every `Z` whose smooth
locus is dense. Since `k̄` is **algebraically closed**, hence perfect, the smooth locus of every
integral `Z` is dense, so this applies to **all** `Z` over an algebraic closure, as in the
  characteristic-zero assertion of Theorem 8.1. The determination
argument is
standard and *not* formalized here (no proof below uses it).

The identification `x ↦ x ⊗ 1` of `ℚ_ℓ(c)` with `ℚ_ℓ` is relative to `ζ`: `CanonicalCycleSystem` is
parametrized by the root system `ζ`, existence is for **every** `ζ`, and the Zarhin input is for
**every** `ζ`.

`CanonicalCycleSystemExists` is the cited existence statement (SGA 4½ Cycle 2.1.2–2.1.3,
2.2.2–2.2.3 (regular-sequence independence), 2.2.6–2.2.10 (determination and all cycles),
2.3.2, 2.3.7–2.3.8; SGA 5 VI 3.2–3.3): a canonical system exists
at every smooth proper `k`-scheme of every relative dimension, field `k`, algebraic closure `k̄` and
prime `ℓ ≠ char k`, with the chart-cover field supplied by EGA IV₄ 17.12.1–2 / SGA 4 VIII 1.1.

## What is proved (the manuscript reductions)

* `IsDivisorProduct`, `IsDivisorProduct.exists_clBar`: a product of `c` divisor classes
  `c1 L₁ ∪ ⋯ ∪ c1 L_c` over `k̄` is the cycle class of the iterated Chern cap
  `c₁(L_c) ∩ ⋯ ∩ c₁(L₁) ∩ [X_{k̄}]` (from `unit`, `chern`);
* `span_clBase_eq_invariants`: if the `Gal(k̄/k)`-invariant classes (Tate classes) are
  `ℚ_ℓ`-combinations of products of divisor classes over `k̄` (the conclusion of Zarhin's Theorem
  8.1, an **input**), the cycle class map `CH^c(X) ⊗ ℚ_ℓ → H^{2c}(X_{k̄}, ℚ_ℓ(c))^{Gal(k̄/k)}` is
  surjective: finite-extension representation (Stacks 0FVQ/0FH6 through
  `ChowFiniteExtension.exists_galoisStage_mem_span_range`, finite Galois stage) followed by
  rational averaging (`AbelianCycleClass.span_range_clBase_eq_invariants`, from the proved Mackey
  formula).
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite Stacks.Chow
  Stacks.EtaleCohomology

universe u

namespace ArithmeticOfJacobiPolynomials

namespace EtaleCycleClassInterface

open AbelianEtale AbelianCycleClass

/-! ### Chow carriers: the geometric Chow group and its finite stages -/

section Carriers

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
  (kbar : Type u) [Field kbar] [Algebra k kbar]

/-- The base change `X_{k̄} = X ×_k k̄`. -/
abbrev geomScheme : Scheme.{u} :=
  pullback f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g

/-- The Chow group `A_i(X_{k̄})` of the base change to `k̄`, over `Spec k̄` (Stacks Chow groups). -/
abbrev geomChow (i : ℤ) : Type u :=
  chowGroup (fieldChowSituation kbar)
    (pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g) i

/-- The Chow group `A_i(X_E)` of the base change to a subextension `E ⊂ k̄`, over `Spec E`. -/
abbrev stageChow (E : IntermediateField k kbar) (i : ℤ) : Type u :=
  chowGroup (fieldChowSituation E)
    (pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k E).g) i

/-- An invertible module on a scheme (a line bundle, the source of a divisor class). -/
structure InvertibleModule (Y : Scheme.{u}) where
  /-- The underlying `𝒪_Y`-module. -/
  L : Y.Modules
  /-- It is invertible. -/
  isInvertible :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.sheaf.obj Y.ringCatSheaf.property L

/-- **The Chern cap `c₁(L) ∩ -  : A_{i+1}(X_{k̄}) → A_i(X_{k̄})`** of an invertible module `L` of
`X_{k̄}`: the Stacks operator `Stacks.Chow.invertibleChernCap` (Tags 02SJ, 02TI) on the Stacks
Chow group. -/
noncomputable def chernCap (L : InvertibleModule (geomScheme f kbar)) (i : ℤ) :
    geomChow f kbar (i + 1) →+ geomChow f kbar i :=
  haveI := L.isInvertible
  (invertibleChernCap (fieldChowSituation kbar)
    (pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g) L.L).capOnChow
    (fieldChowSituation kbar) (pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g) i

/-- **The class of a closed subscheme `ι : Z ⟶ X_{k̄}` in `A_i(X_{k̄})`** (Stacks 02QU, the
associated cycle `[Z]_i`; for `Z` integral of delta-dimension `i` it is the cycle `[Z]`). -/
noncomputable def subschemeChowClass {Z : Scheme.{u}} (ι : Z ⟶ geomScheme f kbar)
    [IsClosedImmersion ι] (i : ℤ) : geomChow f kbar i :=
  QuotientAddGroup.mk' (rationalEquivalences (fieldChowSituation kbar)
    (pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g) i)
    (cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme (fieldChowSituation kbar)
      (pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g) ι i)

/-- A finite subextension is finite-dimensional over `k`. -/
instance (E : FiniteSubextension k kbar) : FiniteDimensional k E.1 := E.2

variable [Algebra.IsAlgebraic k kbar] [CompactSpace X] [QuasiCompact f]

/-- The pullback `A_i(X_E) → A_i(X_{k̄})` from a finite stage (Stacks 0FVQ). -/
noncomputable abbrev stagePullback (E : FiniteSubextension k kbar) (i : ℤ) :
    stageChow f kbar E.1 i →+ geomChow f kbar i :=
  haveI : CompactSpace (Over.mk f).left := ‹CompactSpace X›
  haveI : LocallyOfFiniteType (Over.mk f).hom := ‹LocallyOfFiniteType f›
  haveI : QuasiCompact (Over.mk f).hom := ‹QuasiCompact f›
  (algebraicExtensionSystem k kbar (Over.mk f)).stageChowPullback (op E) i

/-- A class of `A_i(X_E / E)` is a class of `A_i(X_E / k)` (same cycles, same rational
equivalence): the lift `CycleDescent.chowLift` at a finite stage. -/
noncomputable def stageLift (E : FiniteSubextension k kbar) (i : ℤ) :
    stageChow f kbar E.1 i →+ Chow.galoisChowGroup E.1 f i :=
  CycleDescent.chowLift k E.1 f i

end Carriers

/-! ### Cohomology with supports: the Stacks carriers -/

section Supports

attribute [local instance] moduleCat_hasLimitsOfSize
attribute [-instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.etaleSheaves_enoughInjectives

open Stacks.EtaleCohomology.ExtensionTorsor CategoryTheory.Abelian

variable (N : ℕ) {Z Y : Scheme.{u}} (ι : Z ⟶ Y) [IsClosedImmersion ι]

/-- **Cohomology with supports** `H^m_Z(Y, ℤ/N) = Ext^m_Y(ι_* ℤ/N_Z, ℤ/N_Y)` of a closed
immersion `ι : Z ⟶ Y`: the Stacks `Ext` group of étale `ℤ/N`-modules (the carrier of the
library's purity classes, `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.IsPurityClass`). -/
abbrev SupportExt (m : ℕ) :=
  Ext ((etaleModuleDirectImage.{u, 0} (ZMod N) ι).obj (unitSheaf (X := Z) N))
    (unitSheaf (X := Y) N) m

/-- The restriction `ℤ/N_Y ⟶ ι_* ℤ/N_Z` (the unit of `ι^{-1} ⊣ ι_*` composed with
`ι^{-1} ℤ/N_Y ≅ ℤ/N_Z`). -/
noncomputable def restrictUnit :
    unitSheaf (X := Y) N ⟶ (etaleModuleDirectImage.{u, 0} (ZMod N) ι).obj (unitSheaf (X := Z) N) :=
  ((etaleModuleInverseImageAdj.{u, 0} (ZMod N) ι).homEquiv _ _)
    ((etaleModuleInverseImageConstantIso.{u, 0} (ZMod N) ι).app
      (ModuleCat.of (ZMod N) (ULift.{u + 1} (ZMod N)))).hom

/-- **Forgetting supports** `H^m_Z(Y, ℤ/N) → H^m(Y, ℤ/N)`: precomposition with the restriction
`ℤ/N_Y ⟶ ι_* ℤ/N_Z`. -/
noncomputable def forgetSupports {m : ℕ} (γ : SupportExt N ι m) :
    Ext (unitSheaf (X := Y) N) (unitSheaf (X := Y) N) m :=
  (Ext.mk₀ (restrictUnit N ι)).comp γ (zero_add m)

/-- **Restriction of a class with supports to an open `O ⊆ Z`**: the class in
`Ext^m_Y(ι_* j_{O!} ℤ/N, ℤ/N_Y)` obtained by precomposing with the counit
`j_{O!} j_O^{-1} ℤ/N_Z ⟶ ℤ/N_Z` (the form in which the library states local purity,
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.Purity.IsLocalPurityClass`). -/
noncomputable def restrictToOpen (O : Z.Opens) {m : ℕ} (γ : SupportExt N ι m) :
    Ext ((etaleModuleDirectImage.{u, 0} (ZMod N) ι).obj (Purity.localUnit (N := N) O))
      (unitSheaf (X := Y) N) m :=
  (Ext.mk₀ ((etaleModuleDirectImage.{u, 0} (ZMod N) ι).map
    ((etaleModuleExtensionByZeroAdj.{u, 0} (ZMod N) O.ι).counit.app
      (unitSheaf (X := Z) N)))).comp γ (zero_add m)

end Supports

/-! ### The Kummer orientation of a class with supports

A purity class is determined only up to a unit of `ℤ/N`. The canonical class is the one oriented by
the Kummer boundary of the local regular parameters. A **chart** (`KummerChart`) of a closed
immersion `ι : Z ⟶ Y` of a smooth `K`-scheme `Y` is a Zariski open `U ⊆ Y` with `c` functions
`φ₁, …, φ_c ∈ Γ(U, 𝒪_U)` such that

* each closed immersion `i_m : W_m ⟶ U` is the **principal closed subscheme `V(φ_m)`** — the ideal
  sheaf `ker i_m` is the ideal sheaf generated by `φ_m`;
* the scheme-theoretic intersection `Z ∩ U` has ideal sheaf **equal** to `(φ₁, …, φ_c)`;
* `Y` is smooth of relative dimension `r + c` and `Z ∩ U` is smooth of relative dimension `r`
  over `K` — a smooth subscheme of codimension `c` cut out by `c` equations, i.e. the `φ_m` form a
  regular sequence whose differentials are a basis of the conormal module (transverse regular
  parameters);
* `θ` identifies the Kummer flag sheaf with `ι_* j_{!}Λ_{Z∩U}`, compatibly with the units.

On every chart the restriction of the class with supports is the library's *Kummer flag class*
`KummerFlag.kummerFlagClass`, the Yoneda product of the Kummer boundaries `κ(φ_m)` of the units
`φ_m|_{D(φ_m)}`. -/

section Orientation

attribute [local instance] moduleCat_hasLimitsOfSize
attribute [-instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.etaleSheaves_enoughInjectives

open Stacks.EtaleCohomology.ExtensionTorsor CategoryTheory.Abelian KummerFlag

/-- The restriction `Γ(U, ⊤) → Γ(U, V)` of a global function to an open `V`. -/
def restrictFun {U : Scheme.{u}} (φ : Γ(U, ⊤)) (V : U.Opens) : Γ(U, V) :=
  (U.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : V ≤ ⊤)).op).hom φ

/-- **Local parameters `φ₁, …, φ_c ∈ Γ(U, 𝒪_U)` with their principal closed subschemes**: closed
immersions `i_m : W_m ⟶ U` whose ideal sheaf `ker i_m` is *equal* to the ideal sheaf generated by
`φ_m` (`ker_eq`, the scheme-theoretic defining equation `W_m = V(φ_m)`; Stacks ideal sheaves), whose
zero set is the complement of `D(φ_m)` (`range_eq`, a consequence of `ker_eq` recorded because the
library's `KummerFlag.DivisorDatum.ofFunction` takes it). -/
structure ParameterFlag (U : Scheme.{u}) (c : ℕ) where
  /-- The parameters. -/
  φ : Fin c → Γ(U, ⊤)
  /-- The zero schemes. -/
  W : Fin c → Scheme.{u}
  /-- The closed immersions. -/
  i : ∀ m, W m ⟶ U
  [closed : ∀ m, IsClosedImmersion (i m)]
  /-- **`i_m` is the principal closed subscheme `V(φ_m)`**: its ideal sheaf is generated by `φ_m`
  on every affine open. -/
  ker_eq : ∀ (m : Fin c) (V : U.affineOpens),
    (i m).ker.ideal V = Ideal.span {restrictFun (φ m) V.1}
  /-- The basic open `D(φ_m)` is the complement of the zero set. -/
  range_eq : ∀ m, Set.range (U.basicOpen (φ m)).ι.base = (Set.range (i m).base)ᶜ

attribute [instance] ParameterFlag.closed

/-- The ideal sheaf `(φ₁, …, φ_c)` of `U` generated by the parameters. -/
def ParameterFlag.ideal {U : Scheme.{u}} {c : ℕ} (R : ParameterFlag U c) : U.IdealSheafData :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals fun V => Ideal.span (Set.range fun m => restrictFun (R.φ m) V.1)

/-- The Kummer divisor data `(D(φ_m), W_m, φ_m|_{D(φ_m)})` of a parameter flag. -/
def ParameterFlag.datum {U : Scheme.{u}} {c : ℕ} (R : ParameterFlag U c) :
    Fin c → DivisorDatum U :=
  fun m => DivisorDatum.ofFunction (R.φ m) (R.i m) (R.range_eq m)

variable (N : ℕ) {Y : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The map `j_! Λ_U ⟶ Λ_Y` for a Zariski open `j = U.ι : U ⟶ Y` (`j_! Λ_U ≅ j_! j⁻¹ Λ_Y`
followed by the counit). -/
noncomputable def openUnitMap (U : Y.Opens) :
    (etaleModuleExtensionByZero.{u, 0} (ZMod N) U.ι).obj (unitSheaf (X := U.toScheme) N) ⟶
      unitSheaf (X := Y) N :=
  (etaleModuleExtensionByZero.{u, 0} (ZMod N) U.ι).map
      (restrictionUnitSheafIso (N := N) U.ι).inv ≫
    (etaleModuleExtensionByZeroAdj.{u, 0} (ZMod N) U.ι).counit.app (unitSheaf N)

variable {K : Type u} [Field K] {Z : Scheme.{u}} (fY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of K))
  (ι : Z ⟶ Y) [IsClosedImmersion ι]

/-- **A Kummer chart of `ι : Z ⟶ Y` at level `N`, of codimension `c` and relative dimension `r`**
(see the section header). The isomorphism `θ : j_! E_0 ⋯ E_{c-1} Λ_U ≅ ι_* j_{O!} Λ_O` (`j = U.ι`,
`E_m = i_{m*} i_m⁻¹`, `O = ι⁻¹(U)`) is the identity on the units
(`j_! Λ_U → j_! (E_0 ⋯ E_{c-1} Λ_U)` and `Λ_Y → ι_* Λ_Z`; this characterizes `θ`, the unit being an
epimorphism and `j_{O!}Λ_O → Λ_Z` a monomorphism). -/
structure KummerChart (c r : ℕ) where
  /-- The Zariski open. -/
  U : Y.Opens
  /-- The local parameters, with their principal closed subschemes. -/
  R : ParameterFlag U.toScheme c
  /-- `Y` is smooth of relative dimension `r + c` over `K`. -/
  smoothY : SmoothOfRelativeDimension (r + c) fY
  /-- `Z ∩ U` is smooth of relative dimension `r` over `K`. -/
  smoothZ : SmoothOfRelativeDimension r ((ι ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι ≫ ι ≫ fY)
  /-- **Scheme-theoretic transversality**: the ideal sheaf of `Z ∩ U` in `U` is *equal* to
  `(φ₁, …, φ_c)`. -/
  ideal_eq : ι.ker.comap U.ι = R.ideal
  /-- The identification of the flag sheaf with the extension by zero of `Z ∩ U`. -/
  θ : (etaleModuleExtensionByZero.{u, 0} (ZMod N) U.ι).obj (flagSheaf (N := N) R.datum) ≅
    (etaleModuleDirectImage.{u, 0} (ZMod N) ι).obj (Purity.localUnit (N := N) (ι ⁻¹ᵁ U))
  /-- `θ` is the identity on the units. -/
  θ_unit :
    (etaleModuleExtensionByZero.{u, 0} (ZMod N) U.ι).map (flagUnit (N := N) R.datum) ≫ θ.hom ≫
        (etaleModuleDirectImage.{u, 0} (ZMod N) ι).map
          ((etaleModuleExtensionByZeroAdj.{u, 0} (ZMod N) (ι ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι).counit.app
            (unitSheaf (X := Z) N)) =
      openUnitMap N U ≫ restrictUnit N ι

variable {N fY ι}

/-- **The Kummer orientation of a class with supports** `γ ∈ H^{2c}_Z(Y, ℤ/N)` (`Z ⊆ Y` of
relative dimension `r`): on every Kummer chart `(U, φ, θ)` the restriction of `γ` to
`O = ι⁻¹(U)` is the signed Kummer flag class of the parameters transported along `θ`:
`θ ∘ γ|_O = ε^c · ((j_! κ-flag(φ)) ∘ (j_!Λ_U → Λ_Y))`.

The raw library flag uses `kummerUnitClass` (Tag 095L) and Yoneda composition.
Cycle 2.1.2–2.1.3 defines the divisor class as minus the support boundary of the
root torsor. One sign `ε : ℤˣ` relates this convention to Yoneda composition in every codimension
and at every coefficient level. The unit and Chern normalizations use the same cycle map and
divisor classes, so the manuscript's span conclusions hold for either sign. The parameters cut
out the principal closed subschemes scheme-theoretically, as specified in `KummerChart`.
`KummerChartsExist` gives charts over the smooth locus. In positive codimension the Kummer flag
class is nonzero, so a zero class cannot satisfy the orientation there. -/
def IsKummerOriented (ε : ℤˣ) {ζ : K} (hζ : IsPrimitiveRoot ζ N) (hN : IsUnit (N : K)) {c : ℕ} (r
: ℕ)
    (γ : SupportExt N ι (2 * c)) : Prop :=
  ∀ T : KummerChart N fY ι c r,
    (Ext.mk₀ T.θ.hom).comp (restrictToOpen N ι (ι ⁻¹ᵁ T.U) γ) (zero_add _) =
      (ε : ℤ) ^ c •
        (((kummerFlagClass hζ hN (T.U.ι ≫ fY) T.R.datum).mapExactFunctor
          (etaleModuleExtensionByZero.{u, 0} (ZMod N) T.U.ι)).comp
          (Ext.mk₀ (openUnitMap N T.U)) (add_zero _))

end Orientation

/-! ### The canonical system -/

/-- The functoriality package's class on a finite stage, for a `FiniteSubextension`. -/
noncomputable def clStage {B : BigEtaleSite.{u}} {ℓ : ℕ} [Fact ℓ.Prime] [EllAdicSite B ℓ]
    {X : B.Scheme} [IsNoetherian X.1] {k : Type u} [Field k] {f : X.1 ⟶ Spec (.of k)}
    [IsProper f] {kbar : Type u} [Field kbar] [Algebra k kbar] [Algebra.IsSeparable k kbar]
    [Normal k kbar] {c : ℕ} {i : ℤ} (S : CycleClassFunctoriality B ℓ X f kbar c i)
    (E : FiniteSubextension k kbar) :
    Chow.galoisChowGroup E.1 f i →+ etaleCohomologyTwistSpace B ℓ X f kbar c :=
  S.cl E.1

section System

attribute [local instance] moduleCat_hasLimitsOfSize
attribute [-instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.etaleSheaves_enoughInjectives

open Stacks.EtaleCohomology.ExtensionTorsor CategoryTheory.Abelian

variable (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (ℓ : ℕ) [Fact ℓ.Prime] [EllAdicSite B ℓ]
  (X : B.Scheme) [IsNoetherian X.1] {k : Type u} [Field k] (f : X.1 ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsProper f]
  (kbar : Type u) [Field kbar] [Algebra k kbar] [Algebra.IsSeparable k kbar] [Normal k kbar]

/-- `x ∈ H^m(X_{k̄}, ℤ_ℓ) = lim_n H^m(X_{k̄}, ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹)` has `n`-th finite level `e`, an element of
the Stacks `Ext^m(ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹, ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹)` on `X_{k̄}` (`AbelianEtale.levelExtEquiv`). -/
def HasLevel (m : ℕ) (x : (constantLimit B ℓ X f kbar (m : ℤ)).V) (n : ℕ)
    (e : Ext (unitSheaf (X := Stacks.Frobenius.fieldBaseChange (Over.mk f) kbar) (ℓ ^ (n + 1)))
      (unitSheaf (X := Stacks.Frobenius.fieldBaseChange (Over.mk f) kbar) (ℓ ^ (n + 1))) m) :
    Prop :=
  levelExtEquiv B ℓ X f kbar m n (levelProj B ℓ X f kbar (m : ℤ) n x) = e

/-- **The divisor class `c₁(L) ∈ H²(X_{k̄}, ℚ_ℓ(1))` of an invertible module**, given the cycle
class map `cl₁` of divisors (dimension `d - 1`): the cycle class of the Chern cap
`c₁(L) ∩ [X_{k̄}]`, the divisor of a rational section (Stacks Chern cap, Tag 02TI). -/
def divisorClass (d : ℕ) (cl₁ : geomChow f kbar ((d : ℤ) - 1) →+
    etaleCohomologyTwistSpace B ℓ X f kbar 1) (L : InvertibleModule (geomScheme f kbar)) :
    etaleCohomologyTwistSpace B ℓ X f kbar 1 :=
  cl₁ (chernCap f kbar L ((d : ℤ) - 1) (fundamentalChowClass (fieldChowSituation kbar)
    (pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g) ((d : ℤ) - 1 + 1)))

/-- **A canonical `ℓ`-adic cycle class system for `X` of relative dimension `d`.** See the module
docstring for the characterization and the sources. The structure fields are the
carriers (Stacks Chow groups, Stacks `Ext` groups with supports and the library's `ℓ`-adic
cohomology with Galois action) and the numbered normalizations of the cycle class map; existence
is the cited `CanonicalCycleSystemExists`. `k̄` is an algebraic closure of
`k`, separable over `k`. -/
structure CanonicalCycleSystem (ζ : RootSystem ℓ kbar) (d : ℕ) where
  /-- The global comparison sign between support-boundary and raw Yoneda conventions.
  It is a unit of `ℤ`, hence `±1`, fixed across all codimensions and coefficient levels
  (Cycle 2.1.2–2.1.3). -/
  orientationSign : ℤˣ
  /-- `k̄` is algebraically closed (an algebraic closure of `k`, separable over `k`). -/
  isAlgClosed : IsAlgClosed kbar
  /-- The finite-level classes `cl_E`, the class `cl_k` and their functorialities (pullback `π^*`,
  Galois equivariance, invariance of classes of cycles over `k`): SGA 4½ Cycle 2.3.8(ii). -/
  functoriality : ∀ (c : ℕ) (i : ℤ), CycleClassFunctoriality B ℓ X f kbar c i
  /-- The cycle class map of the base change `X_{k̄}` over `Spec k̄`, factoring through
  rational equivalence: SGA 5 VI 3.3(iv), Cycle 2.3.10. -/
  clBar : ∀ (c : ℕ) (i : ℤ),
    geomChow f kbar i →+ etaleCohomologyTwistSpace B ℓ X f kbar c
  /-- **Compatibility with the flat base change `X_{k̄} → X_E`** of every finite stage `E ⊂ k̄`:
  the class of `δ ∈ A_i(X_E)` over `E` is the class of its pullback to `k̄`
  (SGA 4½ Cycle 2.3.8(ii); SGA 5 VI 3.3(i), functoriality of `cl`). -/
  cl_stage : ∀ (c : ℕ) (i : ℤ) (E : FiniteSubextension k kbar) (δ : stageChow f kbar E.1 i),
    clStage (functoriality c i) E (stageLift f kbar E i δ) =
      clBar c i (stagePullback f kbar E i δ)
  /-- **The fundamental class with supports of every integral closed subscheme** `ι : Z ⟶ X_{k̄}`
  of dimension `i` (codimension `c = d - i`): for every level `ℓⁿ⁺¹` a class with supports
  `γₙ ∈ Ext^{2c}(ι_* ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹_Z, ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹)`, which is a local purity class on every open of `Z`
  smooth of dimension `i` over `k̄` (SGA 4 XVI 3.7, 3.9; SGA 5 I 3.1.4), whose image
  under forgetting supports
  is the `n`-th level of an `ℓ`-adic class `x`, and `cl([Z]) = x ⊗ 1` (SGA 4½ Cycle 2.1,
  2.2.10, 2.3.2; Milne LEC Lemma 23.1). -/
  fundamental : ∀ (c : ℕ) (i : ℤ), i + c = d → ∀ (Z : Scheme.{u})
    (ι : Z ⟶ Stacks.Frobenius.fieldBaseChange (Over.mk f) kbar) [IsClosedImmersion ι]
    [IsIntegral Z], schemeDeltaDimension (fieldChowSituation kbar)
      (ι ≫ pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g) = (i : EInt) →
    ∃ (x : (constantLimit B ℓ X f kbar ((2 * c : ℕ) : ℤ)).V)
      (γ : ∀ n : ℕ, SupportExt (ℓ ^ (n + 1)) ι (2 * c)),
      (∀ n, HasLevel B ℓ X f kbar (2 * c) x n (forgetSupports (ℓ ^ (n + 1)) ι (γ n))) ∧
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (O : Z.Opens),
        SmoothOfRelativeDimension i.toNat
          (O.ι ≫ ι ≫ pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g) →
        Purity.IsLocalPurityClass (N := ℓ ^ (n + 1)) ι O (restrictToOpen (ℓ ^ (n + 1)) ι O (γ n))) ∧
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (hN : IsUnit (((ℓ ^ (n + 1) : ℕ)) : kbar)),
        IsKummerOriented (fY := pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g)
          orientationSign (ζ.isPrimitive n) hN i.toNat (γ n)) ∧
      clBar c i (subschemeChowClass f kbar ι i) = twistMk B ℓ X f kbar c x
  /-- **Localized Kummer chart cover.** For
  every integral closed subscheme `ι : Z ⟶ X_{k̄}` of dimension `i` (codimension `c = d - i`), every
  level `ℓⁿ⁺¹` and every open `O ⊆ Z` smooth over `k̄` of relative dimension `i`, every point of `O`
  lies in the open `U ⊆ X_{k̄}` of a `KummerChart`: this is the existence of local regular
  parameters of a smooth subscheme of a smooth scheme (EGA IV₄ 17.12.1–2, SGA 4 VIII 1.1; see
  `KummerChartsExist`). It forces `X_{k̄}` smooth of relative dimension `d` as soon as some such
  chart exists. -/
  charts : ∀ (c : ℕ) (i : ℤ), i + c = d → ∀ (Z : Scheme.{u})
    (ι : Z ⟶ Stacks.Frobenius.fieldBaseChange (Over.mk f) kbar) [IsClosedImmersion ι]
    [IsIntegral Z], schemeDeltaDimension (fieldChowSituation kbar)
      (ι ≫ pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g) = (i : EInt) →
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (O : Z.Opens),
      SmoothOfRelativeDimension i.toNat
        (O.ι ≫ ι ≫ pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g) →
      ∀ z ∈ O, ∃ T : KummerChart (ℓ ^ (n + 1))
        (pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g) ι c i.toNat, ι z ∈ T.U
  /-- The cup product `H^{2a}(ℚ_ℓ(a)) × H^{2b}(ℚ_ℓ(b)) → H^{2(a+b)}(ℚ_ℓ(a+b))`. -/
  cup : ∀ a b : ℕ, etaleCohomologyTwistSpace B ℓ X f kbar a →ₗ[ℚ_[ℓ]]
    etaleCohomologyTwistSpace B ℓ X f kbar b →ₗ[ℚ_[ℓ]]
      etaleCohomologyTwistSpace B ℓ X f kbar (a + b)
  /-- The unit `1 ∈ H⁰(X_{k̄}, ℚ_ℓ)` of the cohomology ring. -/
  one : etaleCohomologyTwistSpace B ℓ X f kbar 0
  /-- **`1` is the image of the identity of `ℤ/ℓⁿ⁺¹`** at every level: the unit is pinned by its
  levels. -/
  one_spec : ∃ x : (constantLimit B ℓ X f kbar ((2 * 0 : ℕ) : ℤ)).V,
    (∀ n, HasLevel B ℓ X f kbar (2 * 0) x n (Ext.mk₀ (𝟙 _))) ∧ one = twistMk B ℓ X f kbar 0 x
  /-- **Unit normalization:** `cl([X_{k̄}]) = 1`, for the fundamental class of `X_{k̄}` in
  dimension `d` (Cycle 2.2.2 and 2.2.4, the empty product at codimension zero). -/
  unit : ∀ j : ℤ, j = d →
    clBar 0 j (fundamentalChowClass (fieldChowSituation kbar)
      (pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g) j) = one
  /-- **Chern normalization:** the class of `c₁(L) ∩ α` is `cl(α) ∪ c₁(L)` for every invertible
  module `L` and every class `α ∈ A_{i+1}(X_{k̄})` of codimension `c`, where `c₁(L)` is the divisor
  class (`divisorClass`): the intersection with a divisor is the cup product with its class (SGA 4½
  statement of SGA 5 VI 3.3(iii); its Cycle 2.3.8(iii), 2.3.9 reference covers the non-excess
  case, and no independent excess proof is claimed). -/
  chern : ∀ (c : ℕ) (i : ℤ) (L : InvertibleModule (geomScheme f kbar))
    (α : geomChow f kbar (i + 1)), i + 1 + c = d →
    clBar (c + 1) i (chernCap f kbar L i α) =
      cup c 1 (clBar c (i + 1) α) (divisorClass B ℓ X f kbar d (clBar 1 ((d : ℤ) - 1)) L)

variable {B ℓ X f kbar}

namespace CanonicalCycleSystem

variable {ζ : RootSystem ℓ kbar} {d : ℕ} (S : CanonicalCycleSystem B ℓ X f kbar ζ d)

/-- The divisor class `c₁(L) ∈ H²(X_{k̄}, ℚ_ℓ(1))` of the canonical system. -/
def c1 (L : InvertibleModule (geomScheme f kbar)) : etaleCohomologyTwistSpace B ℓ X f kbar 1 :=
  divisorClass B ℓ X f kbar d (S.clBar 1 ((d : ℤ) - 1)) L

/-- **The products of `c` divisor classes** `c1 L₁ ∪ ⋯ ∪ c1 L_c ∈ H^{2c}(X_{k̄}, ℚ_ℓ(c))`, with
the empty product `1`. -/
inductive IsDivisorProduct : (c : ℕ) → etaleCohomologyTwistSpace B ℓ X f kbar c → Prop
  | one : IsDivisorProduct 0 S.one
  | mul {c : ℕ} {x : etaleCohomologyTwistSpace B ℓ X f kbar c}
      (L : InvertibleModule (geomScheme f kbar)) :
      IsDivisorProduct c x → IsDivisorProduct (c + 1) (S.cup c 1 x (S.c1 L))

/-- **A product of divisor classes over `k̄` is a cycle class over `k̄`** (from the unit and Chern
normalizations): it is the class of the iterated Chern cap of the fundamental class, a class of
`A_j(X_{k̄})` with `j + c = d`. -/
theorem IsDivisorProduct.exists_clBar {c : ℕ} {x : etaleCohomologyTwistSpace B ℓ X f kbar c}
    (h : S.IsDivisorProduct c x) :
    ∃ (j : ℤ) (α : geomChow f kbar j), j + c = d ∧ S.clBar c j α = x := by
  induction h with
  | one =>
    exact ⟨d, fundamentalChowClass (fieldChowSituation kbar)
      (pullback.snd f (fieldExtensionBaseChangeSituation k kbar).g) d, by simp,
      S.unit d rfl⟩
  | @mul c x L _ ih =>
    obtain ⟨j, α, hj, hα⟩ := ih
    obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ : ∃ i, j = i + 1 := ⟨j - 1, by ring⟩
    have hi : i + 1 + c = d := hj
    refine ⟨i, chernCap f kbar L i α, by push_cast at hi ⊢; omega, ?_⟩
    rw [S.chern c i L α hi, hα]
    rfl

end CanonicalCycleSystem

open CanonicalCycleSystem

/-- **Surjectivity of the cycle class map onto the Tate classes, from geometric divisor-product
generation (Corollary 6.6).** Let `S` be a canonical cycle class system of `X`
of relative dimension `d` and `i + c = d`. If every `Gal(k̄/k)`-invariant class of
`H^{2c}(X_{k̄}, ℚ_ℓ(c))` lies in the `ℚ_ℓ`-span of products of `c` divisor classes over `k̄` (the
conclusion of Zarhin's Theorem 8.1, an input), then the `ℚ_ℓ`-span of the cycle classes of
`A_i(X)` is exactly the invariants.

The proof is the manuscript's: the divisor products are cycle classes over `k̄`
(`IsDivisorProduct.exists_clBar`); the finite combination is represented over a finite Galois stage
`E ⊂ k̄` (Stacks 0FVQ/0FH6, `ChowFiniteExtension.exists_galoisStage_mem_span_range`), where the
classes are classes of cycles on `X_E` (`cl_stage`); rational averaging over the finite Galois
extension `E/k` descends them to `X` (`AbelianCycleClass.span_range_clBase_eq_invariants`). -/
theorem span_clBase_eq_invariants {ζ : RootSystem ℓ kbar} {d : ℕ}
    (S : CanonicalCycleSystem B ℓ X f kbar ζ d) (c : ℕ)
    (i : ℤ) (hi : i + c = d)
    (hTate : ∀ w ∈ (etaleCohomologyTwistRep B ℓ X f kbar c).invariants,
      w ∈ Submodule.span ℚ_[ℓ] {x | S.IsDivisorProduct c x}) :
    Submodule.span ℚ_[ℓ] (Set.range (S.functoriality c i).clBase) =
      (etaleCohomologyTwistRep B ℓ X f kbar c).invariants := by
  refine span_range_clBase_eq_invariants (S.functoriality c i) ?_
  intro w hw
  have hsub : {x | S.IsDivisorProduct c x} ⊆ Set.range (S.clBar c i) := by
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨j, α, hj, hα⟩ := hx.exists_clBar
    obtain rfl : j = i := by omega
    exact ⟨α, hα⟩
  have hw2 : w ∈ Submodule.span ℚ_[ℓ] (Set.range (S.clBar c i)) :=
    Submodule.span_mono hsub (hTate w hw)
  have : IsGalois k kbar := ⟨⟩
  have : CompactSpace (Over.mk f).left := inferInstanceAs (CompactSpace X.1)
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType (Over.mk f).hom := inferInstanceAs (LocallyOfFiniteType f)
  have : QuasiCompact (Over.mk f).hom := inferInstanceAs (QuasiCompact f)
  obtain ⟨E, hE, hwE⟩ := ChowFiniteExtension.exists_galoisStage_mem_span_range k kbar
    (Over.mk f) i (R := ℚ_[ℓ]) (fun α => S.clBar c i α) hw2
  refine ⟨E.1, E.2, hE.to_normal, ?_⟩
  refine Submodule.span_mono ?_ hwE
  rintro _ ⟨δ, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨stageLift f kbar E i δ, S.cl_stage c i E δ⟩

end System

/-! ### The canonical predicate and the cited existence statement -/

section Canon

/-- **`F` is the functoriality package of a canonical cycle class system** of `X`: `F` comes from a
`CanonicalCycleSystem` of relative dimension `d = i + c` (so that `i + c` is the relative dimension
of `X`, the Chow dimension convention). This is the *canonical* selector for
`AbelianArithmetic.CycleClassPredicate`; its existence is the cited `CanonicalCycleSystemExists`. -/
def CanonicalCycleClass (B : BigEtaleSite.{0}) (ℓ : ℕ) [Fact ℓ.Prime] [EllAdicSite B ℓ]
    (X : B.Scheme) [IsNoetherian X.1] {k : Type} [Field k] (f : X.1 ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsProper f]
    (kbar : Type) [Field kbar] [Algebra k kbar] [Algebra.IsSeparable k kbar] [Normal k kbar]
    (c : ℕ) (i : ℤ) (F : CycleClassFunctoriality B ℓ X f kbar c i) : Prop :=
  0 ≤ i + c ∧ ∃ (_ : RelativeDimension f (i + c).toNat) (ζ : RootSystem ℓ kbar)
    (P : CanonicalCycleSystem B ℓ X f kbar ζ (i + c).toNat), P.functoriality c i = F

end Canon

